cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Archival Optical & Radio Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and instrumental provenance
  audits for narrowband radio technosignatures (multi-epoch exoplanet-drift
  de-Doppler with ON/OFF controls), fast photometric glints (TESS pixel-covariance
  qualification), and high-resolution optical echelle laser candidates (ESO HARPS
  and FEROS 1D/2D order and calibration provenance).
authors:
  - family-names: "Andersen"
    given-names: "Martin"
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/andersenmartin-blip/setisearch"
url: "https://github.com/andersenmartin-blip/setisearch"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - SETI
  - technosignatures
  - optical SETI
  - echelle spectroscopy
  - HARPS
  - FEROS
  - narrowband radio signals
  - exoplanets
  - reproducible research
